1 NOTE Ahnentafel position 17.
1 NOTE PARENTAGE CONFIRMED (7 August 2026, PRB-0006 Film 2 triage): Eliza is a daughter of José Cezário de Toledo Lima (P-0054) and Claudina Brandina de Jesus (P-0055), family F-0026. Evidence: the 1879 Matilde inventário (PRB-0006), Film 2 triage, lists her as representante #5 under heir #4 (JC × Claudina). Per 19th-century Brazilian inheritance law, a married woman appeared through her husband as legal representative; item 5 reads "5º Simplicio José Ferreira Armond, cazado com D. Eliza Balbina de Tolledo" — Simplício is named first as her legal actor, Eliza is the heir. A prior session (7 August 2026) misread this as Simplício being JC's son and removed Eliza from F-0026; that correction was itself erroneous and is reversed. The "Simplício José Ferreira de Toledo, solteiro, 14 anos" in the 1867 inventários (PRB-0008 item 6; PRB-0009 item 6) is JC's OWN SON with the Toledo surname — a DIFFERENT person from our Simplício Armond who has the Armond surname.
1 NOTE Recorded three ways: "Eliza Ferreira Armand" (Aristão's 1957 death, CIV-0005), "Eliza Ferreira Toledo" (Marfiza's 1962 death, CIV-0013) and "Eliza Balbina de Toledo" (the 1881 Toledo heir list PRB-0001, as Simplício's wife). All give her the Toledo maiden surname and the owner confirms they are the same woman; the married and maiden forms are both preserved.
1 NOTE Namesake caution (do NOT treat as a variant of Eliza): the 13 November 1880 citation audience in the Ladisláo Toledo estate names "Simplicio José Ferreira Armond e sua mulher Maria Dulcelina de Toledo" — a scribe's slip substituting the name of Eliza's sister Maria Dulcelina de Toledo (a documented child on F-0026) for Eliza. It does not indicate a second wife of Simplício.
