1 NOTE Barbacena locus (1 August 2026): her daughter Carolina's 1821 baptism (PAR-0017, Capela dos Remédios, Piedade da Borda do Campo) places her and her husband Ladisláo at Barbacena in 1821 — the family's origin before the move to the Leopoldina / Fazenda da Concórdia region.
1 NOTE Her parents are now CONFIRMED (5 August 2026) by the 1810 São João del Rei marriage record (PAR-0023, event E-0052): she is the daughter of Alferes Amaro da Silva Xavier (P-0059) and Ignez Francisca de Lima (P-0060), family F-0029. Both parents are described as "naturais e batizados da Freguesia de Barbacena" — born and baptised in Barbacena, consistent with Ladisláo's own Barbacena origin. This resolves the "single open item" flagged after the bounded-negative Barbacena Piedade marriage-book sweep (1793–1822): the couple married at São João del Rei, not Barbacena, explaining the prior negative result. Her own baptism was at Barbacena, 22 March 1795 (Bertioga section), per the secondary Themudo citation — the baptism image has not yet been retrieved. Her parents' own vital records have not been located.
1 NOTE Death date: 12 March 1879. Confirmed from the opening juramento of her own 1879 Leopoldina estate inventory (PRB-0006, folio 6 — already catalogued as PRB-0006): the inventariante Cezário José de Toledo swore on 28 April 1879 that she "faleceu em o dia doze de Março proximo passado." Death event E-0059 created. Her estate was opened six weeks after her death. Grandmother (avó) of the Toledo grandchildren who inherited the Fazenda da Concórdia estate, per the 1877 deed (PRB-0003), the 1881 partilha (PRB-0001), and the 1884 petition (PRB-0002). Eliza Balbina de Toledo (P-0017) is one of those grandchildren. Confirmed alive March 1867: PRB-0009-p5 records her signing the Termo de Louvaçao in person at the Concórdia proceedings. ALSO: the retrieval agent's transcript of the Matilde 1879 inventário (pp.154–155, 2026-08-08) contains a certidão: Capitão Manoel Rodrigues de Lima (São José d'El Rei) donated the enslaved woman Martinha to "minha sobrinha Mathilde Maria de Jesus" — Mathilde is therefore the Capitão's niece. The Capitão bought Martinha from "minha [irmã?] Dona Francisca de Lima" — if "irmã" (sister) is the correct read, Francisca de Lima is the Capitão's sister AND Mathilde's mother, corroborating that Mathilde's mother was Ignez Francisca de Lima (P-0060). The "[maã?/irmã?]" word is uncertain in the transcript and requires image verification.
1 NOTE Intervening generation NAMED (1 August 2026) by her own 1879 Leopoldina estate inventory (PRB-0006): Eliza's parent is Mathilde's son José Cezário de Toledo Lima (P-0054, heir #4, ⚭ D. Claudina), so Mathilde is now linked to Eliza (P-0017) through the structured edge F-0027 (Mathilde ⚭ Ladisláo Egydio Ferreira de Toledo, P-0056) → F-0026 (José Cezário ⚭ Claudina). This supersedes the earlier prose-only grandmother link and resolves her deliberate orphan status. Her husband (Eliza's great-grandfather) is Ladisláo Egydio Ferreira de Toledo (P-0056).
1 NOTE 30 July 2026 (Full-Text via research/from-retrieval/, ARK 3:1:3QHJ-1QWB-7BYX, catalogued as PRB-0004): a second Concórdia / Ribeirão de São Bento Toledo deed names Mathilde's husband, Ladisláo Egydio Ferreira de Toledo, and a parent couple below them, Antonio Zeferino de Toledo and Dona Maria Perpétua ("seus finados avós Dona Mathilde Maria de Jesus e Ladisláo Egydio Ferreira de Toledo e seus paes e sogros Antonio Zeferino de Toledo e Dona Maria Perpétua"). Antonio Zeferino is thus a son of Mathilde × Ladisláo. RESOLVED (1 August 2026) by the full inventory (PRB-0006): Antonio Zeferino de Toledo × Maria Perpétua are heir #3 (Eliza's UNCLE and aunt), NOT Eliza's parents — corroborated on folio 8 ("de M.a Perpetua nº 3"). Antonio Zeferino is recorded as a documented sibling of José Cezário on F-0027. The two same-named "Ladisláo Egydio Ferreira de Toledo" are also resolved: the elder is Mathilde's husband (P-0056); the "solteiro de 23 annos" grantor grandchild is heir #4's son (Eliza's brother, documented on F-0026).
1 NOTE Namesake caution (do NOT conflate): a different "Mathilde Maria de Jesus" — widow of Generoso Fernandes de Moura, with children surnamed de Moura — appears in a Republic-era Moura inventory (ARK 3:1:3QHK-QQ2X-VS4Y) in the same retrieval drop. She is unrelated to this P-0027 (wife of Ladisláo Egydio de Toledo).
