1 NOTE Father of João Muniz Bittencourt (P-0019); hence Antenor Muniz's Azorean great-great-grandfather. His own 1866 Povoação death (PAR-0015 → events E-0047, E-0048) is the primary record for him: a landowner (proprietário) of Nossa Senhora Mãe de Deus, Povoação, Ilha de São Miguel (Açores, Portugal), resident at Lomba do Botão, who drowned at sea off the Garajau on 24 July 1866 aged 46 (born c.1820), intestate, leaving eight children. It names his wife Francisca Roza do Espirito Santo (P-0047, family F-0020) and his parents João Muniz Bytancourt (P-0048) and Maria Jacintha de Medeiros (P-0049, family F-0023).
1 NOTE Name correction: João's 1915 Carangola óbito (PAR-0007) recorded the father as "Manoel Luiz Bittencourt", but his own Povoação death (PAR-0015) gives the true name "Manoel Muniz Bytancourt" — the Azorean spelling of the family surname (Brazilianised to "Bittencourt" by his son). The erroneous "Manoel Luiz Bittencourt" form is preserved as a source variant.
1 NOTE Nationality now asserted as Portuguese: although PAR-0015 does not state Manoel's own naturalidade, his parents are "naturaes desta freguesia" of Povoação, his son João was confirmed "natural da Ilha de São Miguel", and he lived and died in the parish — so a São Miguel (Açorean) birth is secure.
