1 NOTE BORER II in the Imigrantes de Nova Friburgo compilation (Henrique Bon), distinct from Jacob Borer (P-0050, BORER I), who originates from Erschwil and held Casa/Lote 70/56. Laurent originates from Grindel and held Casa/Lote 73/86. The two families shared the Heureux Voyage but were allocated different lots and are not proven to be closely related. The compilation states "não há evidência de parentesco próximo entre os dois grupos."
1 NOTE Father named as "certo Jacob Borer, de Grindel, Soleure" in the compilation (PUB-0003). The qualifier "certo" reflects the compiler's own hedged confidence in this attribution. The Grindel parish register images in the retrieval drop show a "Joannes Borer × Ana Maria Werli" baptising a daughter in 1782 — a strong lead for Laurent's parentage but not yet confirmed as the same individual. No parent family in this repository; the father is noted here only.
1 NOTE Emigrated to Brazil in 1819 on the ship Heureux Voyage. Settled at Nova Friburgo, Rio de Janeiro, occupying Casa 73, Lote 86. Married Anna Maria Werhly (P-0069) on 03/07/1820 at Nova Friburgo. Probably died in the vale do Macaé area, Nova Friburgo; date of death unknown.
