1 TITL Grindel (Solothurn) Catholic parish baptism register, 1751–1753 — baptism of Johann Jacob Wehrli (17 January 1751) and Johann Joseph Wehrli (23 June 1752), children of Johannes Wehrli × Barbara Alleman
1 TEXT Grindel (Solothurn) Catholic parish baptism register, page 571, contains two baptism entries for children of Johannes Wehrli (P-0074) and Barbara Alleman (P-0075): Johann Jacob Wehrli, baptised 17 January 1751 (entry 2 on the page), and Johann Joseph Wehrli, baptised 23 June 1752 (entry 6). The Johann Jacob entry is PRIMARY evidence for the birth date (17 January 1751, Grindel) and parentage of P-0072 (Johann Jacob Wehrli), upgrading from the secondary Raibert Wehrli blog to a confirmed, primary record. The godfather at the 1751 baptism is Hans Jacob Heggendorn — the same Heggendorn family that appears in the 1782 Grindel marriage register (Catharina Heggendorn as Jacob Borer's wife, per the 1781–1784 Grindel register). The June 1752 entry for Johann Joseph Wehrli confirms the couple's continued residence in Grindel.
