1 TITL 1867 Concórdia probate inventory of Ladisláo Egídio Ferreira de Toledo — título de herdeiros confirming eight children including Francisco Leocádio (item 4, deceased before Ladisláo) and José Cesário Lima (item 8, deceased), with JC's children including a son named Simplício Ferreira de Toledo (item 6, distinct from Simplício Armond P-0016) and a declaration on Claudina Brandina de Jesus
1 TEXT The 1867 Concórdia (Districto do Rio Pardo, MG) probate inventory of Ladisláo Egídio Ferreira de Toledo (P-0056). Its título de herdeiros (gen1) lists Ladisláo's eight children by Mathilde Maria de Jesus (P-0027), including: child #4 Francisco Leocádio de Toledo (P-0061), who predeceased Ladisláo and was married to Maria Joaquina de Jesus (P-0062); and child #8 José Cesário de Toledo Lima (P-0054, deceased), represented by his children. Page p2 continues with JC's nine representantes, listing a son named Simplício as item 6 ("Simplicio José Perrura [Ferreira] de Tolledo, Solteiro de quatorze annos") — independently corroborating PRB-0008 that JC had a son of this name. IMPORTANT: this Simplício is JC's OWN SON with the Toledo surname (b. ~1853, 14 years old and solteiro in 1867, dead before 1879 when he does not appear in PRB-0006) — a DIFFERENT person from Simplício José Ferreira ARMOND (P-0016, Eliza's husband). Page p2 also declares: "a mae destes Dona Claudina Brandina de Jesus é viúva, cuja [morte do] marido falleceu depois do Inventariado" — correctly read as: JC (Claudina's husband) died after Ladisláo; Claudina was alive on 7 March 1867 (PRB-0008 p5 confirms her physical presence as inventariante). Pages 3–5 record the herdeiros citation list, the Termo de Louvaçao (10 March 1867), and signatures including Mathilde Maria de Jesus (alive March 1867) and Narciso Marques Braz as proxy for several heirs. A person named "Simplicio Jaci Ferrura [Ferreira] de Toledo" appears on p4 as curator of Ladisláo's minor orphan heirs — NOTE: this person has the Toledo surname, not Armond; whether this is P-0016 or a different family member requires image verification (see limitations). The curator of JC's minor heirs was Aureliano de Sales Toledo (JC's sibling, item 5), before the same judge (Dr. Mortimário de Sousa Lintz) as PRB-0008.
